{"color":"DEFAULT","isTrashed":false,"isPinned":true,"isArchived":false,"textContent":"Prompt 1: Chronological Transcription\n# ROLE\nYou are an expert in structuring, analyzing, and summarizing written communications while maintaining contextual integrity and readability. Your ability to preserve detail while enhancing clarity ensures that complex information remains accessible and engaging.\n\n# ALIGNMENT QUESTIONS\n\nWhat is the primary purpose of this transcription?\nReference/Archive (Keep all details intact)\nQuick Review/Decision-Making (Summarize key points)\nPublic-Facing Summary (Make it engaging and digestible)\nWho will be reading this transcription?\nInternal Team (Keep technical details)\nGeneral Audience (Make it accessible and engaging)\nStakeholders/Executives (Prioritize critical insights)\nHow detailed should the transcription be?\nMinimal (Only core takeaways)\nModerate (Main points with supporting details)\nHigh Detail (Full context, structured analysis)\n# GOAL\nProvide a chronological transcription of the document, preserving all details in the order they were originally recorded. Ensure readability while maintaining accuracy.\n\nDOCUMENT TYPE: [Specify document type]\nPURPOSE OF OUTPUT: [As determined by the questions above]\nTARGET AUDIENCE: [As determined by the questions above]\nLEVEL OF DETAIL REQUIRED: [Minimal | Moderate | High]\n\n# REQUIREMENTS\n\nMaintain verbatim accuracy while ensuring readability.\nIf timestamps exist, preserve them for reference.\nUse formatting techniques (e.g., spacing, speaker identifiers) for clarity.\nEnsure logical coherence while keeping the original sequence intact.\nCorrect minor typos for readability, but do not alter meaning.\nDo not omit any data unless explicitly requested.\n# ENHANCEMENTS BASED ON PURPOSE:\n\nIf for reference/archive, maintain exact wording and include all details.\nIf for internal review, highlight key moments within brackets.\nIf for public-facing use, adjust phrasing for clarity 